Slf4j:
------
slf4j stands for simple logging facade for java which acts as a facade that means as a abstraction layer on your logging framework.

The main use of this slf4j is that we can change the underlying logging framework at any time without disturbing the code:

Basically we create loggers using Logger logger=LoggerFactory.getLogger(Class.class);

logger.info("hi");
logger.Debug("hhfhf");
etc.

=============================================================================================================
Log4j2 is the succesive version of log4j. It provides many features like;
1. Asynchronous logging, it makes use if lmax disruptor which work seamlessly in the application without blocking the threads.
2. It is garbage free logging that means not that much temporary logger object created.
3. It provides multiple appenders like files, console, database etc.
4. Supports XML, JSON, YAML, and properties for configuration.
5. Dynamic reloading of configuration without restarting the application.
6. plugin Architecture: extensible using the plugins for custom filters, appenders.

